  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>b</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>c</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>d</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>:</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math>. Define <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>det</mo><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;for all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>M</mi></math>&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Z</mi></math> is set of all integers. Then the number of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>M</mi></math> such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></math>&nbsp;is equal to&nbsp;<u>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</u>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "16",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>.<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></math></p><p>where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Case <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>:</mo></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi></math> possible pairs are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;</p><p>For&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi></math> possible pairs are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;</p><p>So,&nbsp;total number of matrices in case&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p><p>Case <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi><mo>:</mo></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p>Similarly, total number of matrices in case&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p><p>Hence, total number of matrices&nbsp;are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn></math>.</p>",
